EMPLOYMENT WITH MAINSTAY
c) Employment at Will
Mainstay strives to provide a positive work environment and a solid economic foundation
upon which all employees may build a future. However, Mainstay is also cognizant that
employees and management alike sometimes initiate personnel changes. In this regard, it
is expressly understood that employment with Mainstay is at-will; it is for no specific
duration and shall continue only so long as it is mutually agreeable to you and Mainstay.
As an at-will employee, either the employee or Mainstay may terminate employment, with
or without cause, and at any time. No section of this Handbook is meant to be construed,
nor should be construed, as establishing anything other than an employment-at-will
relationship, nor does it limit management's discretion to make personnel decisions such
as hiring, reassignment, change of wages and benefits, promotion, demotion, termination,
or discipline. Moreover, no one in the organization, other than the CEO or Chief People
Officer of Mainstay, has the authority or legal ability to modify the at-will nature of the
employment relationship. The CEO or Chief People Officer can do so only if it is clearly
set forth in a written agreement that is signed by both the CEO or Chief People Officer
and the employee in question.
d) Equal Employment Opportunity
Mainstay is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits all forms discrimination against
applicants and employees. It is Mainstay’s policy and practice to provide equal
employment opportunity to all qualified individuals in both personnel and employment
practices including, but not limited to, recruiting, hiring, promotion, placement, transfer,
training, compensation, fringe benefits, demotions, layoffs, and/or termination.
Accordingly, Mainstay prohibits discrimination of applicants and employees based on
age, ancestry, color, marital or domestic partnership status, AIDS/HIV status, height,
weight, reproductive health decision-making, medical condition, physical or mental
disability, military or veteran's status, national origin, ancestry, race (including traits
historically associated with race such as hair texture and protective hairstyles), religion or
creed (including observance and practice and religious dress and grooming practices),
sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, breastfeeding or medical conditions related to
breastfeeding, and medical conditions related to pregnancy, childbirth or breastfeeding),
gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic
characteristics/information, protective order status, unfavorable discharge from military
service, citizenship status, arrest record, expunged or sealed convictions, or any other
basis protected by federal, state or local law or ordinance or regulation, or any other
consideration made unlawful by federal, state, or local laws. Mainstay also prohibits
unlawful discrimination based on the perception that anyone has any of those
characteristics, or is associated with a person who has or is perceived as having any of
those characteristics.
7
Additionally, Mainstay provides equal pay for employees who perform substantially
similar work unless the difference in pay is due to seniority, merit, a system that measures
production, and/or a bona fide factor other than sex, race, or ethnicity, as permitted
under applicable law. Mainstay prohibits paying employees less on the basis of their sex,
race or ethnicity.
Any discrimination violates this policy even if it does not rise to a violation of applicable
law. Mainstay’s commitment applies to all persons involved in Company operations and
prohibits unlawful discrimination of any applicant or employee (including, without
limitation, unpaid interns) by any employee of Mainstay, including supervisors, managers
and coworkers.
Any manager or supervisor who receives a complaint or otherwise becomes aware of
discriminatory conduct must report the conduct to the People Team at
mainstay-hr@mainstay.io so that an investigation can be made and corrective action
taken, if appropriate.
e) Standards of Conduct
Mainstay values teamwork and ethical conduct. As a business, we follow all applicable
laws and regulations. As an employee, we expect you to do the same. Every employee
has the duty and the responsibility to be aware of and abide by existing rules and
policies.
Additionally, Mainstay is responsible for providing a safe and secure workplace and
strives to ensure that all individuals employed with the Company are treated in a
respectful and fair manner. The Company expects all employees to abide by certain work
rules of general conduct and performance at all times. In addition, any misconduct off the
job that affects the Company’s ability to run its business or the employee’s ability to
perform their job may be a valid reason for corrective action or progressive discipline.
Regardless of your classification, status, or length of service, you are expected to meet
and maintain our standards for job performance and behavior. Although there is no way
to identify every possible violation of standards of conduct, the following is a partial list of
infractions:
● Conduct which may endanger the wellbeing of any employee or other person
on Company premises.
● Falsifying any employment document, filing a false claim of worker’s
compensation or harassment.
● Engaging in any kind of illegal activity while on Company time or on Company
premises.
● Engaging in acts of dishonesty, fraud, theft, or sabotage.
● Performance which does not meet the requirements of the position, including
