WORKING AT MAINSTAY
Maintaining good attendance is a condition of employment and an essential job function
of each employee’s job. Because Mainstay depends heavily upon its employees, it is
important that employees report to work as scheduled. Dependability, attendance,
punctuality, and a commitment to do the job right are essential at all times.
Employees are expected to work on all scheduled workdays, during all scheduled work
hours, and to report to work on time, except when they take approved time off from work
or a leave of absence protected by law. Employees are expected to follow proper
notification procedures if they will be late, absent or need to take time away from work
during the course of their normal work schedule. This notification does not excuse the
occurrence rather it simply notifies the manager. For unforeseeable occurrences,
employees must notify their manager as soon as practicable, and no later than their
scheduled starting time at work, absent extenuating circumstances. Employees are
expected to follow proper procedures for requesting planned absences from work.
Excessive absenteeism or tardiness may result in discipline, up to and including
termination of employment, at management’s discretion. Termination for violation of this
policy may lead to a denial of unemployment benefits. Absences protected by law will not
be considered for purposes of assessing excessive absenteeism or tardiness.
