Mainstay generally permits employment of family members and consensual romantic
relationships between employees. Employees who are or become family members, or
employees who are in a supervisor/subordinate relationship and establish a consensual
romantic relationship, must notify the People team promptly by connecting with the
People Team or emailing hr@mainstay.io.com. In the context of this policy,
“supervisor/subordinate relationship” is broadly defined as one in which a person
oversees and directs the work done by others.
Mainstay makes all hiring decisions on the basis of the qualifications. If the applicant is
a relative of an employee or involved in a consensual romantic relationship with an
employee, the applicant and employee must inform the Company prior to any
employment consideration. Failure to notify the company may disqualify the applicant
from consideration.
The family member or individuals romantically involved with an employee may not be
hired for a position if employment would have any of the following effects:
