n) Offsite Policy
At Mainstay, we value bringing teams together to foster collaboration, spark innovation,
and strengthen relationships through impactful offsites. These gatherings are designed to
align teams across all levels, driving strategic planning and collective success. To
maximize impact, offsites should be strategically scheduled around planning cycles to
align on goals, reflect on progress, and chart the path forward.
What does Mainstay define as an offsite?
An offsite is a dedicated gathering of one or more teams for an extended period to
achieve business objectives and strengthen team collaboration and culture. These
sessions are a vital part of our success as an early-stage startup, providing uninterrupted
time for focused collaboration, strategic planning, and outcome-driven discussions.
To ensure the time is productive and well-utilized, teams are expected to define clear
objectives and desired outcomes prior to booking and attending an offsite. This
preparation helps maximize the value of these gatherings, fostering innovation and
alignment across all levels of the organization.
How often should teams expect to have offsites at Mainstay?
We aim for every employee to attend at least one offsite annually to create space for
meaningful collaboration and creative thinking. However, we understand that the
25
frequency and structure of offsites may vary based on team goals, roles, and business
needs.
How do I know which type of offsite to plan?
Planning an offsite can be challenging, as there are several factors to consider. To ensure
your offsite is impactful, it’s important to review these considerations during the planning
process and determine whether a virtual or in-person format best suits your team’s
needs.
●
●
Key Considerations
●
Timing: Offsites should be strategically scheduled to precede or follow strategic
planning cycles. Additional offsites may be scheduled when there are significant
shifts in business strategy or needs.
Attendee Selection: Team leads should carefully consider who should attend
based on the offsite's objectives and the potential impact on day-to-day
operations.
Duration: The length of the offsite should be determined based on the agenda and
goals, balancing productivity with time away from regular duties.
In-Person or Virtual: Decide when an offsite is necessary, vs. a virtual alternative,
based on objectives and team needs.
Eligibility
All full-time employees are eligible to attend offsites. Contractors and part-time
employees will be invited to attend if specified by the senior leadership team for a specific
event.
