c) Passwords
All passwords must meet Mainstay’s password length, complexity and composition
requirements, which are outlined in the Password Policy. Employees should not reuse any
of their previous six passwords, nor create a password that is overly similar to their
previous six passwords. At no time should an employee share, disclose, or otherwise
display their passwords to anyone.
Passwords used to access documents or files must be encrypted during electronic
transmission. For the transmission of a password protecting confidential information, the
username/file must be sent via a different medium than the password. For example, if a
password protected document containing confidential information is emailed to a person,
the password cannot be provided over email, but must be provided via phone, text, or
38
another secure medium.
For the transmission of a password protecting Restricted information, the username/file
must be sent via a different medium than the password, and the password shall be broken
in two parts and sent by two different mediums. For example, if a password protected
document containing Restricted information is sent via email, the password must be
broken in two parts and provided by two different mediums such as phone and Slack, or
text and phone.
Password Expiration
Passwords for all account types must be changed in cases when a user no longer has a
business requirement to access the account, when a user leaves the organization, or
when a compromising event is suspected, reported, or confirmed, whichever is earliest.
