h) Volunteer Time Off (VTO)
Mainstay values community service and believes it’s important to give back to the
communities in which we operate. We encourage all regular employees to spend up to
eight (8) hours per year on community service, which can be tracked as paid Volunteer
Time Off (VTO). Any use of VTO must be approved by the employee’s manager with two
weeks advance notice of taking the time off.
Our team members should use this time to assist the non-profit organization(s) of their
choice. We encourage teams to consider using this time together as it can also be a great
way to bond and team-build. Whether it’s building a home through Habitat for Humanity
or serving a meal at a local homeless shelter, these experiences help connect us to our
communities and remind us about the importance of giving.
All regular employees are provided eight (8) VTO hours to be used throughout the
calendar year with a minimum increment of four (4) hours. Any unused VTO hours will not
carry over from year to year and will not be paid out upon termination of employment.
i) Voting Time Off
Mainstay believes that it is the responsibility and duty of employees to exercise the
privilege of voting in elections. In accordance with this philosophy, the company will grant
its employees approved time off to vote if necessary due to work schedules and for
periods of service as an election official.
Although polls are open for extended hours, we realize that in some instances some
employees’ work schedule may make it difficult for them to vote during polling hours. This
policy applies to tribal, municipal, county, state, and federal elections.
In such an event, the employee is expected to work with their direct manager at least two
weeks prior to taking paid time off, to allow for three (3) consecutive hours to vote, unless
otherwise provided by applicable state law. The manager has discretion in determining
whether the time taken will be provided at the beginning or ending of the employee’s shift.
All Mainstay employees are provided up to eight (8) hours of paid voting time off to use
throughout the year to encourage participation in their respective communities, unless
applicable state law requires greater benefits.
As a civil volunteer of your local community if you are wanting to participate in voting poll
events, volunteer time off can be applied for these instances. Please refer to the
Volunteer Time Off policy for eligibility requirements. Voting Time Off may be used in
increments of 1 hour, and any unused time will not be paid out upon termination of
46
employment. Please direct all inquiries about this policy to the People Team at
hr@mainstay.io.
j) Jury & Witness Duty
Mainstay recognizes that employees may be called to serve jury duty or witness leave.
Employees will receive regular pay for a maximum of forty (40) hours pay in accordance
with state guidelines while serving jury duty or witness leave. Upon receipt of notification
from the state or federal courts of an obligation to serve on a jury or to act as a court
witness, you should notify your manager & People Team by providing copies of the
subpoena or jury summons.
Once the People Team receives your documentation they will input the hours into Rippling
on your behalf and save any documentation in your Rippling profile.
Any additional jury duty leave that is not required to be paid under the Jury and Witness
Duty policy or applicable state law will be unpaid.
The Company shall not discharge, discipline or otherwise penalize an employee because
the employee is absent for the purpose of attending jury duty or if employee is absent for
the purpose of attending a judicial proceeding in response to a subpoena or other court
order or process which requires the attendance of the employee at the judicial
proceeding, provided that the employee gives advance notice to the Company of the
expected absence to the extent permitted by applicable law. The provisions of this
section do not apply if you are absent from work to attend a judicial proceeding as a
criminal defendant.
k) Voluntary Unpaid Time Off
Mainstay is subject to seasonal trends as well as other macroeconomic conditions that
can cause business volume to increase or decrease for short and extended periods of
time. When volume is projected to be low, hourly team members will be offered the
opportunity to take advantage of voluntary time off (VTO) either by logging fewer hours
on their timesheet or by using an existing PTO balance.
Eligible employees must be compensated hourly, have approval from their manager and
use no more than sixteen (16) hours of unpaid VTO per month. The availability of VTO will
be based on regional needs, subject to partner forecasts and may not be available to all
employees on a single team as employees may cover different regions.
l) Bereavement
Mainstay is supportive of you and your family through life’s challenging times. If a loved
one has passed, we want you to have time away from work to heal from your loss,
including the loss of an unborn child. Our bereavement time off provides up to ten (10)
47
consecutive days of paid time off in the event of the death of the employee's spouse,
domestic partner, child, stepchild, parent, stepparent, parents in law, siblings and step
siblings. These days can be taken consecutively or non-consecutively. If bereavement
time is taken non-consecutively, please make sure you make arrangements with your
manager prior to taking bereavement time so that business processes are not disrupted.
You are also entitled to two (2) consecutive days of paid time off in the event of the death
of other close family members and loved ones.
Bereavement time off must be requested and approved in advance by your manager
unless advance notice and approval is not possible. In such a case, notice must be given
as soon as possible. Please notify the People Team the dates bereavement will be taken
and the team will input your time into Rippling.
The start of your paid bereavement time should be taken within 30 days of notice of
death, unless there are outstanding circumstances that will need to be discussed and
approved by your manager. If bereavement time cannot be taken within 30 days, please
notify your manager and the People Team. Bereavement days do not carry over from
calendar year to calendar year and are not paid out upon employment termination.
Any employee who falsifies information to obtain paid time off under this Policy will be
subject to disciplinary action up to and including termination.
