reinstatement if business circumstances have changed such that the employee would
have lost the position even if the employee had not taken Paid Parental Leave (e.g., if the
employee’s position is no longer available due to job elimination). In the event that the
employee’s original position is not available, the employee will be offered a substantially
similar position, if available, for which the employee is qualified. If the employee declines
to accept this similar position, they will be deemed to have resigned. To the extent
permitted by applicable law, if no substantially similar position is available for which the
employee is qualified, the employee’s employment will be terminated.
