the provisions of the FMLA. If the employee’s leave extends beyond the employee’s FMLA
leave entitlement or the employee does not return at the expiration of the FMLA leave
period, employment may be terminated.
j) Intermittent Leave
If medically necessary, FMLA leave occasioned by a serious health condition may be
taken intermittently (in separate blocks of time due to a serious health condition) or on a
reduced leave schedule (reducing the usual number of hours an employee works per
workweek or workday). FMLA leave may also be taken intermittently or on a reduced
leave schedule for a qualifying exigency relating to covered military service. This leave
will be monitored by the People Team.
k) Substitution of Paid Leave for Unpaid Leave
FMLA is generally unpaid leave, however non-exempt employees may use their sick leave
balance or accrued PTO time and exempt employees may use their sick leave balance
and/or up to 10 days of FTO while taking FMLA leave. Under these circumstances, both
the paid and unpaid leave count as Family and Medical Leave. FMLA leave will run
concurrently with worker’s compensation leave.
l) FMLA Medical Certification
The Company will inform employees if leave will be designated as FMLA protected and
the amount of leave counted against the employee’s leave entitlement. Ineligible
employees will be provided a reason for the ineligibility. If the Company determines that
the leave is not FMLA protected, the Company will notify the employee.
Returning from Leave
If you take leave because of your own serious health condition (except if you are taking
intermittent leave), in some circumstances you may be subject to provide medical
certification that you are fit to resume work.
This policy is adopted to meet Mainstay’s legal obligations in providing leaves of
absences and is not intended to expand employees’ legal rights to time off. The Company
intends to administer the policy in accordance with applicable legal requirements. Certain
states require employers to provide greater or different job-protected leave. When
applicable, the Company complies with all such leave laws. When leave provided under
one of these laws is covered under the federal FMLA, it also shall count toward the
58
employee’s federal FMLA entitlement and as FMLA Leave under this policy, to the extent
permitted under applicable law. Any leave provided by Mainstay that is not legally
required is at the sole discretion of management and does not impose any legal duty
upon Mainstay.
m) Disability Leave (including pregnancy)
Mainstay’s Short-term Disability (STD) benefit provides time off with 100% salary
continuation plus certain benefits for a defined period when an employee is unable to
perform their work duties due to a serious health condition caused by an illness or injury
that involves treatment by a physician. If the illness or injury is work related, then it may
qualify for worker’s compensation and not short-term disability. Eligibility requirements
are as follows:
• Must be a regular employee working at least 20 hours per week.
• Eligible on date of hire and automatically enrolled – this is an employer paid
benefit and there are no employee contributions.
• The illness or injury must be for more than seven continuous days for it to
qualify as a disability, otherwise employees may use sick leave for any time off
needed.
In addition to the above eligibility, for an employee to be considered disabled, the health
condition must be certified by a physician and approved by Mainstay’s third-party
disability provider. Examples of disabilities include:
• In patient care in a hospital or medical care facility
• Continuing treatment by a physician
• Pregnancy
Employees may be eligible for up to eight (8) weeks of STD benefits at 100% base salary
and 60% of base salary continuation, up to a maximum of $2,500 per week, for weeks 9
to 12 of a disability. The benefit is subject to an elimination period which is seven (7) days.
Payment begins on the 8th day of illness/injury. Employees must use their accrued sick
and/or PTO/FTO for the first five business days. STD benefits may run concurrently with
other federal & statutory leave benefits such as FMLA, etc.
n) Coordination with Other Benefits/Policies
Family Medical Leave Act (FMLA) - FMLA provides up to 12 weeks of unpaid,
job-protected leave for specific family and medical reasons including an employee’s
illness/injury. STD runs concurrently with FMLA and will be counted toward the 12 weeks
of available FMLA leave per 12-month period. If an employee is eligible for FMLA,
Mainstay’s third-party provider will automatically begin the FMLA claim at the same time
as the STD claim. All other requirements and provisions under the FMLA will apply. Please
refer to the FMLA policy for additional information on FMLA.
59
• State Leaves – Several states in the US have independent STD benefits. In
some cases, these leaves will run concurrently with Mainstay’s STD policy
and in other cases they may run independently. The third party provider will
provide information on which state leave an employee is eligible for and
instructions on how to apply.
• Health Benefits - Benefits will continue and the employee portion of the
premium will be deducted from their paychecks once they return to work, in
accordance with applicable law.
• Long Term Disability – Once an employee exhausts their short-term disability
leave – which is a maximum of 12 weeks, the employee may be eligible for
long term disability (LTD). Mainstay’s third-party provider will assist the
employee with the LTD claim if they qualify for the benefit. If an employee is
on LTD, they will be placed on unpaid leave and receive salary continuation
directly from Mainstay’s LTD provider. An employee can be on LTD for an
unlimited time, but their Mainstay health benefits, and employment will
continue for a maximum of 6 months.
• Vacation - Employees will continue to accrue vacation during paid short-term
disability leave. If an employee has extended their leave with long term
disability or unpaid leave, vacation accruals will cease until they return to
work.
• Holidays - STD supersedes any Mainstay scheduled holiday, if a holiday occurs
while an employee is on leave, the entire week is counted as a week of STD
leave.
State and local laws may provide leave benefits in addition to what is provided under this
policy. If you have questions regarding paid parental leave or associated state law leaves,
please refer to the state specific addendum or contact the People Team at
hr@mainstay.io.
o) Unpaid Personal Leave (UPL)
A leave of absence without pay (unpaid personal leave) may be granted to employees
which can be used to travel, rest, pursue non-work interests, or other personal reasons.
Employees must have 12 months of continuous service in order to be eligible for unpaid
personal leave and must be in good standing (must meet expectations of their current
role and level) at the time they request the leave. In partnership with the People team, the
employees' supervisor will review and approve the request based on business needs.
Eligible employees may take an unpaid personal leave of up to six (6) continuous weeks.
Mainstay benefits will continue as usual during your unpaid personal leave. You will be
required to pay the unpaid premiums upon your return to work. Premiums will be doubled
(current deductions owed plus one extra deduction) once you return to work for each pay
period until the outstanding balance is paid in full, unless otherwise prohibited under
applicable law.
60
Employees must email hr@mainstay.io with the appropriate approvals, start and end
dates of personal leave.
p) Leave to Accommodate a Legally Recognized Disability
In addition to leave provided under the FMLA and corresponding state laws, leave may be
available if necessary to reasonably accommodate employees with a workplace injury or
a qualified disability under state, local and/or federal law. Such leaves are generally
unpaid, although you may be eligible for workers’ compensation insurance benefits,
Company-sponsored disability insurance benefits, or state disability insurance wage
replacement benefits (where available). Employees must substitute any accrued paid sick
leave for unpaid leave. In addition, regular, eligible exempt employees may use up to 15
workdays of Flexible PTO during unpaid leave, and eligible non-exempt employees may
substitute any accrued PTO for unpaid leave; however, all accrued sick leave must be
used by the employee before they may use Flexible PTO or accrued PTO. Whether such
leave is available depends on the circumstances of each particular case. Please contact
the People Team at hr@mainstay.io for specific details.
q) Leave for Victims of Domestic Violence, Crime, Sexual Assault & Stalking
A victim of domestic violence, sexual assault or stalking, or a crime that caused physical
injury, or mental injury and a threat of physical injury, may take unpaid time off to get help
to protect their health, safety, or welfare or the health, safety or welfare of their child or
household member, including time off to:
● undergo treatment for physical or mental injuries or abuse;
● seek medical attention for injuries;
● obtain services from a domestic violence shelter, program, rape crisis center,
or victim services organization or agency;
● obtain psychological counseling;
● receive or participate in safety planning related to domestic violence, sexual
assault or stalking; and
● take other actions to increase safety from future domestic violence, sexual
assault, stalking, or other crime, including temporary or permanent relocation,
or a temporary or permanent restraining order, injunction or other judicial
relief or related legal advice.
In addition to the above reasons for leave, employees may take leave permitted by
applicable state or local law if the employee’s qualifying family member was a victim of a
qualifying crime, domestic violence, sexual assault, harassment and/or stalking.
The employee must provide their supervisor reasonable advance notice of the intention
to take time off, unless advance notice is not feasible. The request for time off must be
supported with appropriate documentation. If advance notice is not feasible, the
employee must provide their supervisor documentation within a reasonable time following
the absence. The documentation must certify the reason for the absence in a manner that
61
meets applicable legal standards. If notice is not provided in accordance with the
requirements of the law, the time off will be considered unauthorized. Accrued paid sick
leave may be used in conjunction with this leave.
An employee who is the victim of domestic violence, sexual assault or stalking may also
request a reasonable accommodation in the workplace to ensure the employee’s safety.
The Company will work with the employee to determine what reasonable
accommodations can be made. Reasonable accommodations may include putting in
locks, changing the employee’s shift or phone number, transferring or reassigning the
employee, or help with keeping a record of what happened to the employee. The
Company may require a signed statement from the employee certifying that the request is
for a proper purpose, and may also require proof showing the employee’s need for
accommodation, in accordance with applicable law. The Company will not tell an
employee’s coworkers or anyone else about an employee’s request for reasonable
accommodation under this policy, except as required to implement any accommodation.
The Company will not retaliate or discriminate against any employee who is a victim of
domestic violence, sexual assault, stalking, or who exercises any right provided under
this policy.
r) Military Leave
Mainstay provides military leave to employees who serve in the uniformed services as
required by the Uniformed Services Employment and Reemployment Rights Act of 1994
(USERRA) and applicable state laws. Regular full-time and part-time employees who are
members of the National Guard, Civil Air Patrol or the U.S. Armed Forces reserve unit are
eligible for military leave.
Upon receipt of an active duty order or absence for voluntary or involuntary uniformed
service, you should notify your manager and the People Team with as much advance
notice as possible.
s) Pay During Military Leave
Mainstay will pay your regular earnings for a maximum of fifteen (15) workdays in a
calendar year, unless otherwise specified under applicable state law. In addition, exempt
employees will continue to receive their full salaries for any weeks in which they perform
any work for the Company. If military leave exceeds fifteen (15) workdays, the remainder
of leave will be unpaid, unless otherwise specified under applicable state law. During
unpaid military leave, non-exempt employees may use available PTO hours and exempt
employees may use up to 10 days of FTO, unless otherwise specified by current state law.
In order to receive the continuation of pay from the company or available PTO or FTO
hours, a copy of your military orders must be provided to the People Team. If you do not
elect to receive pay from the company or use available PTO, you are not required to
62
submit a copy of your orders and will be on unpaid leave for the duration of our military
service.
t) Extended Active Duty
Mainstay will pay your regular earnings for a maximum of fifteen (15) workdays in a
calendar year, unless otherwise specified under applicable state law. In addition, exempt
employees will continue to receive their full salaries for any weeks in which they perform
any work for the Company. If military leave exceeds fifteen (15) workdays, the remainder
of leave will be unpaid, unless otherwise specified under applicable state law. During
unpaid military leave, non-exempt employees may use available PTO hours and exempt
employees may use up to 10 days of FTO, unless otherwise specified by current state law.
In order to receive the continuation of pay from the company or available PTO or FTO
hours, a copy of your military orders must be provided to the People Team. If you do not
elect to receive pay from the company or use available PTO, you are not required to
submit a copy of your orders and will be on unpaid leave for the duration of our military
service.
u) Reemployment Rights
Employees who have reemployment rights under USERRA shall be reemployed in the
position they would have held had they remained continuously employed at Mainstay, if
they are qualified for such a position or can become qualified for it with reasonable effort.
Otherwise they shall be returned to the same position they held prior to military service. If
returning from extended active duty, a copy of your military orders must be provided to
the People Team.
Upon return to active employment with the Company, an employee has up to three (3)
times the period of service, not to exceed five (5) years, to make up missed employee
contributions in the 401(k) retirement plan. Annual deferral limits determined by the IRS
do apply. If the period of extended active duty spans multiple calendar years, the
employee designates the specific year or years their make up contributions cover.
An employee’s period of active duty shall represent continuous employment service as
long as the military service conforms to provisions specified in USERRA.
Because the USERRA and state law is detailed, comprehensive, and complex, you should
contact the People Team with additional questions regarding your rights and
responsibilities under the USERRA and state military leave laws. Please see the People
Team if you have any questions regarding your eligibility for this leave. Employees
requesting leave for military duty should contact the People Team to request leave as
soon as they are aware of the need for leave. For request forms and detailed information
on eligibility, employee rights while on leave and job restoration upon completion of leave,
contact the People Team.
63
v) Additional Leave Policies
The Company provides time away from work consistent with all applicable stated, federal,
and local laws, including, for example, state or local laws providing for school activities
leave, civil air patrol leave, emergency responder leave, volunteer firefighter leave, leave
for blood donation, leave for bone marrow donation, leave for organ donor leave, leave
for military spouses, military leave, leave for victims of domestic violence, sexual assault
or stalking, leave for parents and guardians who are required to attend the juvenile court
proceedings or leave to participate in a literacy or rehabilitation program, some of which
are further explained in the state-specific addenda to this Handbook. Time off that is
provided under applicable laws will ordinarily be unpaid except where the law requires
that it be compensated. Please contact the People Team at hr@mainstay.io for
information about additional leave policies.
Emergency Leave
Mainstay will also provide up to 5 days of paid leave for unforeseeable emergency events
per incident, or as required by applicable law. This emergency Leave will be reviewed on
a case by case basis, so please reach out to your manager or email hr@mainstay.io if you
have any questions pertaining your eligibility for this type of leave.
Some examples eligible for this type of leave include but not limited to the following:
● Natural disasters (i.e: hurricane, storms, blizzards, flooding,
fires)
● Lack of power and running water due to unforeseeable natural
events
● Public Health Emergency
● Evacuation of affected areas
● Property damage due to natural disasters
● Hazardous Materials Accident
● Chemical/Biological/Radiological Emergencies
● National Emergencies (War, Terrorism, etc)
